   "about": "Assesses Japan’s wartime production capacity, resource supplies and transport constraints in 1943.",
   "summary": "The report argues that Japan controls ample raw materials but lacks the shipping and processing capacity for rapid industrial expansion; merchant ship losses are its most immediate constraint. Its transportation analysis estimates fleet capacity and examines rail networks and proposed continental links. Tables and discussion assess oil stocks and refining, steel capacity and alloy supplies, followed by broader raw-material shortages and surpluses. The section ends during an assessment of electric generating capacity, consumption and prospects for expansion.",
